<title>USA: Bruno's Q3 Oct 26 shr loss widens. [CORRECTED 23:38 GMT]</title>
<headline>Bruno's Q3 Oct 26 shr loss widens. [CORRECTED 23:38 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr    loss     $2.45	   loss   $0.47</p>
<p> Net    loss     61,700	  loss   26,000</p>
<p> Sales	     694,200		  655,200</p>
<p>(Corrects sales for Q3 to Oct 26 1996)</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  n/a			n/a</p>
<p>	   9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr    loss     $2.26	   loss   $0.26</p>
<p> Net    loss     56,700	  loss   18,200</p>
<p> Sales	     2,147,000		2,087,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  n/a			n/a</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Full company name is Bruno's Inc</p>
<p>NOTE: The third quarter and first nine month 1996 included an unusual $89 million in costs associated with the sale of the company's Vidalia operations.  </p>
<p>The company later said there were 25.2 million shares outstanding for the third quarter and first nine months 1996 compared to 70.4 million shares outstanding for the third quarter and first nine months 1995.</p>
<p>The 1995 figures included shares in the old company, before a leveraged buyout by KKR Associates in August 1995, Bruno's said.</p>
